<title>USA: Rohm and Haas Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>Rohm and Haas Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pct</p>
<p>							 1997    1996 Change</p>
<p> Net sales					    $986    $994 (1%)</p>
<p> Share of affiliate net earnings (losses)	3     (3)    -</p>
<p> Income taxes					   51	54  (6)</p>
<p> Net earnings					  104     100   4%</p>
<p>Net earnings applicable to common shareholders</p>
<p>							   102	98    4</p>
<p>Net earnings per common share (in dollars)</p>
<p>							  1.62    1.46  11%</p>
<p>Average common shares outstanding (000's)</p>
<p>							62,976  67,099  ---</p>
<p>(in millions of dollars, except per-share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: EPS increase reflects repurchase of six percent of outstanding common shares during the past year. The repurchase had a positive effect of $0.10 per share on 1997 Q1 earnings.</p>
<p>The company estimated that its 1997 Q1 EPS would have been $0.10 higher if the European and Japanese currency effects had been neutral.</p>
</text>
